s/title: A Baumslag-type second letter makes the shift tape over Q\(t_1, t_2, \.\.\.\) finitely presented, its localization/title: A Baumslag-type second letter makes the shift tape Z[t_v] ⋊ Z^2 finitely presented, its localization over Q(t_1, t_2, ...)/;
s/---\n\n\*\*ESTABLISHED \(2026-09-18\)\*\* through\n`k-infinity-lies-in-a-simple-localization-of-an-fp-ring-proof`\. Lane proof,\nelementary\. It is the ring analogue of Baumslag's finitely presented\nmetabelian group; no priority is claimed\./artifacts:\n  - research\/artifacts\/gq-referee-a-k-infinity-lies-in-a-simple-localization-of-an-fp-ring.md\n  - research\/artifacts\/gq-referee-b-k-infinity-lies-in-a-simple-localization-of-an-fp-ring.md\n---\n\n**ESTABLISHED (2026-09-18)** through\n`k-infinity-lies-in-a-simple-localization-of-an-fp-ring-proof`. Lane proof,\nelementary; refereed PASS by `gq-referee-a` (proof gaps) and `gq-referee-b`\n(citations and scope), nits applied. No priority is claimed.\n\n**Precursor.** Baumslag's group `Γ = <a, s, t | [a, a^t], [s, t], a^s = a a^t>`\n(G. Baumslag, Proc. Amer. Math. Soc. 35 (1972) 61--62) is finitely presented, so\nits group ring `Z[Γ] = Z[V] ⋊ Z^2` is too, with `Z[V]` a Laurent ring in\ncountably many variables. Localizing gives `Q(u_v) ⋊ Z^2 ≅ K_∞ ⋊ Z^2`. So the\nfirst two items are one step from Baumslag's theorem; the tape `T` below is\nthe additive variant, with `x ↔ t` and `y ↔ s` in his letters./;
s/The third, with the second, forces all\n   conjugates of `t` to commute, by the induction behind Baumslag's group\./The third, with the second, forces all\n   conjugates of `t` to commute, by the induction behind Baumslag's group./;
s/   field `K_∞`\. It contains `K_∞`\./   field `K_∞` (for skew group rings over commutative rings see P. Öinert,\n   arXiv:0904.4661, Theorem 6.13: simple iff `G`-simple and maximal commutative).\n   It contains `K_∞`./;
s/  `y t y\^-1 = t \+ t_1` reduces them to one, as `a\^t = a a\^s` does for\n  Baumslag's group\./  `y t y^-1 = t + t_1` reduces them to one, as `a^s = a a^t` does for\n  Baumslag's group./;
s/By the\n  diagonal-subfield bound of Attempt 3 on\n  `countable-char-zero-fields-embed-in-fp-simple-rings`, the base carrying them\n  must have infinite Krull dimension\./For Leavitt--Nekrashevych completions, the\n  diagonal-subfield bound of Attempt 3 on\n  `countable-char-zero-fields-embed-in-fp-simple-rings` says a copy of `K_∞` in\n  the diagonal needs a base of infinite Krull dimension. The alternative is a\n  non-diagonal commutative subring./;
